1
00:00:00,789 --> 00:00:02,634
This video is for the lab team.

2
00:00:02,634 --> 00:00:08,823
You will learn how to receive cases from the clinics, move each work through its stages, use an external

3
00:00:08,823 --> 00:00:10,489
lab, and send the work back.

4
00:00:10,940 --> 00:00:15,070
Sign in with your name and password. You land on the Lab board.

5
00:00:16,552 --> 00:00:21,425
Every case from the nurses appears here. The chips filter by stage:

6
00:00:21,425 --> 00:00:25,862
new, in work, at an external lab, ready to send, and overdue.

7
00:00:26,313 --> 00:00:33,088
Each card shows the file number, the doctor, the clinic, the scan date and the due date, and every work

8
00:00:33,088 --> 00:00:34,403
with its own status.

9
00:00:34,854 --> 00:00:39,654
When the case reaches you, tap Receive. Then tap Start work when you begin.

10
00:00:40,647 --> 00:00:44,133
If the work goes to an outside lab, tap External lab.

11
00:00:44,133 --> 00:00:48,737
Choose the lab, the expected return date, and the cost if you know it.

12
00:00:49,187 --> 00:00:54,777
When the work is finished, tap Ready. The nurse and the doctor are notified right away.

13
00:00:55,228 --> 00:00:59,768
Then tap Send to clinic. The nurse confirms receipt from her page.

14
00:01:00,219 --> 00:01:05,689
iTero cases have their own tag with the iTero case number, so you can match the scan quickly.

15
00:01:06,140 --> 00:01:13,318
When the nurse sends a case directly to an external lab, it shows with a purple tag: External lab, FYI only.

16
00:01:13,318 --> 00:01:17,040
The case left the clinic, but it is not directed to you.

17
00:01:17,491 --> 00:01:24,231
Tap Details to see the full timeline of a case: who did each step, and when. You can also write a note here.

18
00:01:24,682 --> 00:01:29,672
To find a case, type the patient file number or the case number in the search box.

19
00:01:30,123 --> 00:01:37,993
Lab KPIs show the average turnaround, on-time rate, redo rate, external work and its cost, and the overdue work.

20
00:01:38,444 --> 00:01:45,664
That's it. Update every case as soon as it moves, so the clinics always know where their work is. Thank you!
